  <!-- Regulatory family (Vol.1 §Regulatory Signs p.21–24 / Vol.2 App.3 R01–R83). Bodies are
       STATED and always draw: prohibitory = white disc / red ring / black symbol + red slash
       (R01 red-outlier, R47/R48 blue ground, R51/R52 black border); mandatory = blue disc /
       white border / white symbol; priority = Stop octagon + Give-Way point-down triangle.
       Codes + .1=left / .2=right mirror pairs follow Vol.1 p.8. Only pages whose interior is
       drawn for real (R01 bar, R41/R42/R65/R71/R72/R75/R76 arrows, R46/R49/R52 figures,
       R47/R48/R51 crossbars) or reuses an existing glyph (R05/R08/R09/R81/R82/R83), or is
       flagged with exactly one honest SYMBOL_UNRESOLVED placeholder (figurative vehicle / horn
       silhouettes), are registered — so no shipped R plate renders an empty disc.
       R21–R25/R44/R73/R74/R77, R63/R64 and the temporary variants are held back (see S9 report). -->
